# AEGIS — AI-Enabled Enterprise Document Management System

AEGIS (AI-Enabled Enterprise Document Management System) is a full-stack document management platform designed to securely store, organize, manage, and retrieve enterprise documents.

The system combines **role-based access control, document permissions, activity tracking, secure authentication, and AI-powered document interaction using RAG** into a single application.

## Features

- Secure user authentication with JWT
- Role-based access control
- Document upload and management
- Document-level permission management
- Document search and filtering
- Document metadata management
- Activity and audit tracking
- User and role management
- Notifications
- AI-powered document assistant
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for document-based question answering
- PDF text extraction and document chunking
- Vector embeddings for semantic retrieval
- Ollama-based local LLM and embedding integration
- Responsive web interface
- Contact and access-denied pages
- Secure configuration using environment-specific properties

## Technology Stack

### Backend
- Java
- Spring Boot
- Spring Security
- Spring Data JPA / Hibernate
- REST APIs
- JWT Authentication
- Maven

### Frontend
- React
- JavaScript
- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vite

### AI / RAG
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
- Ollama
- LLM integration
- Text embeddings
- Semantic retrieval
- PDF text extraction
- Document chunking

### Database
- Relational database
- JPA / Hibernate
- Separate database configuration for application and RAG data

### Development & Tools
- Git & GitHub
- Postman
- Maven
- npm

## System Architecture

AEGIS follows a layered full-stack architecture:

```text
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │      React UI        │
                    │      Frontend        │
                    └──────────┬───────────┘
                               │ REST APIs
                               ▼
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │    Spring Boot       │
                    │      Backend         │
                    ├──────────────────────┤
                    │ Controllers           │
                    │ Services              │
                    │ Security / JWT        │
                    │ Repositories           │
                    └───────┬───────┬───────┘
                            │       │
                ┌───────────┘       └──────────────┐
                ▼                                  ▼
       ┌─────────────────┐                ┌─────────────────┐
       │   Application   │                │   RAG Pipeline  │
       │    Database     │                │                 │
       └─────────────────┘                │ PDF Extraction  │
                                          │ Chunking        │
                                          │ Embeddings      │
                                          │ Retrieval       │
                                          │ LLM Generation  │
                                          └─────────────────┘
RAG Pipeline

The AI assistant processes enterprise documents through a Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipeline:

Document Upload
      ↓
PDF Text Extraction
      ↓
Text Chunking
      ↓
Embedding Generation
      ↓
Vector Storage
      ↓
Semantic Retrieval
      ↓
Relevant Context
      ↓
LLM
      ↓
Context-Aware Answer

This allows users to ask questions about their documents while grounding responses in the available document content.

Security

AEGIS implements multiple layers of application security:

JWT-based authentication
Spring Security
Role-based authorization
Document-level permissions
Protected API endpoints
Separation of application secrets from source control
Configurable JWT signing secret
Access-denied handling

Sensitive configuration such as database credentials and JWT secrets is intentionally excluded from the repository.

