Running Locally
Prerequisites

Make sure the following are installed:

Java
Maven
Node.js and npm
A relational database
Ollama, if using the local AI/RAG functionality
Backend

Navigate to the backend:

cd DMS

Configure your local application.properties using the provided:

application.properties.example

Then run:

./mvnw spring-boot:run

On Windows:

mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
Frontend

Open another terminal:

cd dms-frontend
npm install
npm run dev

The Vite development server will provide the frontend URL in the terminal.

Configuration

The repository contains example configuration files for required environment-specific settings.

For the backend, create:

DMS/src/main/resources/application.properties

using:

DMS/src/main/resources/application.properties.example

Do not commit real credentials, JWT secrets, database passwords, or other sensitive configuration.

